    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0326" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/518</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-18T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 18,
                                1918, 3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[For Morris:]</p>
                <p>Your October 13, 5 p.m. Department would like to urge acceptance of plan at once
                    upon Japanese Ambassador here, but does not understand or see necessity for
                    phrase in Article 2, “who shall be appointed by the senior military officers of
                    the Allied forces in the several districts occupied by them.” Time presses for
                    early settlement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
